# Arc UI

## Morrow precedence

The project instructions, root `DESIGN.md`, and `docs/handoff/2026-11-24/current/UIARC-INTEGRATION.txt` override conflicting stock guidance below. For Stitch-derived UI, read `.agents/rules/stitch-to-morrow.md` before implementing or reviewing. shadcn/Base UI remains the baseline; reuse fitting approved components. Introduce Arc only after the repository's component review. Use Morrow's light neutral/lime tokens, DM Sans, specified weights, radii, and route-appropriate widths. Do not import stock foundation CSS globally until its selectors and overlapping variables have an inspected Morrow theme bridge. Preserve existing visible keyboard focus; foundation import is not a prerequisite for focus styling. Centralized Arc adaptation is permitted where a wrapper/theme cannot reach the necessary style. Retain dependency, accessibility, state, and reduced-motion checks. This amendment does not authorize visual conversion or new components outside an approved phase.

When building or polishing UI, follow the Arc skill at `.claude/skills/arc/` (start with `SKILL.md`). Prefer Arc components and blocks over hand-rolled UI.

**Discover:** Use the Arc MCP (`arc` / `https://uiarc.dev/api/mcp`) with `search_components` and `get_component`. If auth fails, ask the user to reconnect. Without MCP, use `https://uiarc.dev/llms.txt` and `https://uiarc.dev/components/<id>/markdown`.

**Install:** `npx shadcn@latest add @uiarc/<id>` (needs `@uiarc` registry in `components.json`). Import `@/components/arc/foundation.css` once in the root layout after install. Do not rebuild Arc items from scratch or reconstruct Pro source.

## Always

1. Use an existing Arc component or block before writing UI. Read "When not to use" before choosing an item.
2. Use only documented props. Compose and wrap Arc components; never fork or restyle their internals.
3. One page container per app. Blocks fill their column with no second gutter or max width.
4. One `h1`, one primary button per surface (`button` defaults to `variant="primary"`; set `secondary` or `ghost` on the rest), one memorable detail per view.
5. Semantic tokens only: `--background`, `--surface`, `--surface-muted`, `--foreground`, `--text-secondary`, `--text-muted`, `--border`, `--accent`, `--success`, `--warning`, `--danger`, `--radius-*`, `--text-*`, `--space-*`.
6. Accent marks active, selected, progress, and emphasized data. Status colors only for real status, with a label.
7. Type: Geist for headings 30px and up, Inter for the rest, weights 400 and 500 only, sizes from the scale, `tabular-nums` for changing numbers.
8. Nested corners are concentric: inner radius = outer radius - padding.
9. Motion from `@/components/arc/lib/motion-tokens`: `spring.smooth` for panels and state, `spring.snappy` for presses, `spring.morph` for shared highlights. Animate transform and opacity only; always include a reduced-motion branch.
10. First render is server-safe (no `window`, `localStorage`, `Date.now()`, or `Math.random()` output). Animated elements keep stable keys.
11. Every data region has loading (`skeleton`), empty (`empty-state`), error (inline `alert`), and in-place success states.
12. Check 390, 768, 1024, and 1440px: no sideways scroll, wide tables scroll inside their card, touch targets at least 44px.

## Never

- Eyebrow labels or overlines above headings; all caps or uppercase transforms.
- Em dashes in copy. Use a period, comma, colon, or parentheses.
- Hand-made focus rings or any ring on pointer focus. Keyboard focus uses Arc's `:focus-visible` from `foundation.css`.
- Raw hex, Tailwind color classes, weights above 500, or arbitrary font sizes on Arc surfaces.
- Decorative gradients, glows, colored shadows in components; icons in rounded tiles; nested decorative cards.
- A toast as the only confirmation of a foreground action.
- Motion that loops without meaning or replays on every scroll.

Before finishing UI work, run `.claude/skills/arc/checklist.md` and fix until it passes.
